        <briefdescription>
<para>Searches <computeroutput>splits</computeroutput> and returns the <computeroutput>limit</computeroutput> highest-scoring rows among the candidates that they return. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The result holds global row ids and iterates them in ascending order; pass it to <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_scan_context_builder_1a85b99415dcb3179120a380353425fe0e" kindref="member">ScanContextBuilder::SetGlobalIndexResult()</ref></computeroutput> to read the rows, whose scores the read returns in the <computeroutput>_INDEX_SCORE</computeroutput> field.</para>
<para>The splits are searched in parallel, and each one returns at most <computeroutput>limit</computeroutput> candidates, chosen by its index. Ties among the candidates are broken by ascending row id, but which of the rows tied at the <computeroutput>limit</computeroutput>-th score of a split become candidates is up to its index. A split ranks only its search row ranges, and with deletion vectors enabled only the rows that are live in the snapshot the splits were planned from; BM25 statistics still come from its whole index shard. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>splits</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Splits planned by a <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_full_text_scan" kindref="compound">FullTextScan</ref></computeroutput> of the same column, all from one snapshot. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The rows found, or an error if a split is invalid, its index files do not index the column of the latest schema (for example, after the column was replaced), or an index cannot be read. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
